  "text_md": "## 4. Embedded Toric Resolution\n\nThe rational double point singularities are given by one of the following equations:\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nRemark 4.1 . Each member of ADE -singularities is Newton non-degenerate.\n\nEmbedded toric resolutions of ADE -singularities were studied in [18, 19]. Here differently we construct regular refinements of Gr¨ obner fans of each members of them. This leads us their embedded toric resolutions [1, 2]. Additionally, these resolutions will be minimal which means that:\n\nDefinition 4.2 . An embedded toric resolution is called minimal if\n\n- i ) The vectors in the regular refinement are irreducible.\n- ii ) The resolution graph obtaining from the refinement does not have any -1 curve means the self-intersection of each vertex is different from -1 (this gives us the resolution graph is minimal).\n\nNote that the self-intersection of a vertex is computed as: The number -s ∈ Z ≤ 0 with s.v = ∑ m i =1 v i is called the self-intersection of the vertex v in the graph where each v i is adjacent to v in the regular refinement.\n\n## 4.1. A n -singularities. Consider the hypersurface X = V ( f ) ⊂ C 3 where\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nGiven v 1 ∈ ( R ≥ 0 ) 3 , let In v 1 ( f ) = f . The polyhedral cone associated with v 1 is\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nGiven v 2 ∈ ( R ≥ 0 ) 3 , let In v 2 ( f ) = xy . The polyhedral cone associated with v 2 is\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nGiven v 3 ∈ ( R ≥ 0 ) 3 , let In v 3 ( f ) = -z n +1 . The polyhedral cone associated with v 3 is\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nThe Gr¨ obner fan G ( X ) of X and its Gr¨ obner cones can be seen as\n\nFigure 1. The Gr¨ obner fan and its Gr¨ obner cones for A n -singularities\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n(0\n\n, n\n\n+1\n\n,\n\n1)",
